<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S1.F1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S1.F1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The original set of 8 “master key filters”, obtained by applying a clustering technique to
the receptive fields learned from depthwise-separable deep networks,
as extracted by Babaiee <span id="S1.F1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">et al.</span>
(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeyear"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">2025a</a></cite>), “through greedy search
on the ConvNeXt v2 Tiny model” developed by Liu <span id="S1.F1.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">et al.</span> (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeyear"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">2022</a></cite>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
