<section id="S2.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.1.3 </span>Spatial spread measures applied to zero-order pure difference operators</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we will in the modelling and the analysis stages
primarily consider the following non-centered
first-order difference operators
(see Figure <a href="#S2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 2.1.2 Spatial spread measures applied to first-order scale-space kernels ‣ 2.1 Spatial spread measures for characterizing the spatial extent and the spatial offset of receptive fields ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> for an illustration):</p>
<table id="S2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{x+}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m+1,n)-h(m,n),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{x+}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m+1,n)-h(m,n),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{x-}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m,n)-h(m-1,n),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{x-}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m,n)-h(m-1,n),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{y+}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m,n+1)-h(m,n),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{y+}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m,n+1)-h(m,n),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{y-}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m,n)-h(m,n-1),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{y-}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m,n)-h(m,n-1),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the following centered first-order difference operators:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{x}h)(m,n)&amp;=(h(m+1,n)-h(m-1,n))/2,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{x}h)(m,n)&amp;=(h(m+1,n)-h(m-1,n))/2,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{y}h)(m,n)&amp;=(h(m,n+1)-h(m,n-1))/2.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{y}h)(m,n)&amp;=(h(m,n+1)-h(m,n-1))/2.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Additionally, in the following interpretations of the results
to be considered in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Interpretation of the analysis and modelling results in terms of scale-space theory for spatial receptive fields ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>,
we will also consider the following centered second-order difference operators:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{xx}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m+1,n)-2h(m,n)+h(m-1,n),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{xx}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m+1,n)-2h(m,n)+h(m-1,n),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{xy}h)(m,n)&amp;=(h(m+1,n+1)-h(m+1,n-1)\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{xy}h)(m,n)&amp;=(h(m+1,n+1)-h(m+1,n-1)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;-h(m-1,n+1)+h(m-1,n-1))/4,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;-h(m-1,n+1)+h(m-1,n-1))/4,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{yy}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m,n+1)-2h(m,n)+h(m,n-1).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}(\delta_{yy}h)(m,n)&amp;=h(m,n+1)-2h(m,n)+h(m,n-1).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For the non-centered first-order difference operators,
we specifically have the following concerning their spatial mean values:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}M(|\delta_{x+}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}+\tfrac{1}{2}\\
0\end{array}\right),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}M(|\delta_{x+}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}+\tfrac{1}{2}\\
0\end{array}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}M(|\delta_{x-}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}-\tfrac{1}{2}\\
0\end{array}\right),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}M(|\delta_{x-}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}-\tfrac{1}{2}\\
0\end{array}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}M(|\delta_{y+}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}0\\
+\tfrac{1}{2}\end{array}\right),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}M(|\delta_{y+}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}0\\
+\tfrac{1}{2}\end{array}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}M(|\delta_{y-}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}0\\
-\tfrac{1}{2}\end{array}\right),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}M(|\delta_{y-}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}0\\
-\tfrac{1}{2}\end{array}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">while for the centered first-order or second-order difference operators, <math id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{*}\in\{\delta_{x},\delta_{y},\delta_{xx},\delta_{xy},\delta_{yy}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{*}\in\{\delta_{x},\delta_{y},\delta_{xx},\delta_{xy},\delta_{yy}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
because of their pure mirror symmetries or anti-symmetries,
their spatial mean values are all zero:</p>
<table id="S2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(|\delta_{*}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}0\\
0\end{array}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(|\delta_{*}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}0\\
0\end{array}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">For the non-centered first-order difference operators,
we specifically have the following concerning their spatial variances:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}V(|\delta_{x+}|)=V(|\delta_{x-}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}\tfrac{1}{4}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{array}\right),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}V(|\delta_{x+}|)=V(|\delta_{x-}|)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}\tfrac{1}{4}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{array}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
