<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S2.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The result of computing the responses to the monomials <math id="S2.T2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{00}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{00}=1</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S2.T2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{10}=x-m_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{10}=x-m_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.T2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{01}=y-m_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{01}=y-m_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> for the 8 “master key filters” shown in
Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, where the spatial offset <math id="S2.T2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{x},m_{y})^{T}=M(|h(\cdot,\cdot)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{x},m_{y})^{T}=M(|h(\cdot,\cdot)|</annotation></semantics></math>
represents the spatial mean of the absolute value of each filter.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
