<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="S2.F5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Graphs of the error measure <math id="S2.F5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\det V(|h_{i}(\cdot,\cdot)-C_{i}|)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\det V(|h_{i}(\cdot,\cdot)-C_{i}|)}</annotation></semantics></math>
for <math id="S2.F5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{7,8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.890em" minsize="0.890em">{</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.890em" minsize="0.890em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{7,8\}</annotation></semantics></math> when determining the DC compensation constants
<math id="S2.F5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{7}\approx-0.0118" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.0118</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{7}\approx-0.0118</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.F5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{8}\approx-0.0386" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.0386</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{8}\approx-0.0386</annotation></semantics></math> according
to (<a href="#S2.E71" title="In 2.4 Reducing the bias in the estimates of the spatial variance of the Gaussian-smoothing-like receptive fields by DC-compensation ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>), in order
to later renormalize the Gaussian-like “master key filters” to unit <math id="S2.F5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm,
as regular Gaussian kernels obey.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
