<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S2.T4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The result of computing the discrete <math id="S2.T4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm <math id="S2.T4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|h(\cdot,\cdot)\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h(\cdot,\cdot)\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>
as well as the discrete spatial mean value <math id="S2.T4.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M(|h(\cdot,\cdot))|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(|h(\cdot,\cdot))|</annotation></semantics></math> according to
Equation (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.1 Spatial spread measures for characterizing the spatial extent and the spatial offset of receptive fields ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) and the discrete spatial variance <math id="S2.T4.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V(|h(\cdot,\cdot))|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(|h(\cdot,\cdot))|</annotation></semantics></math>
according to Equation (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.1 Spatial spread measures for characterizing the spatial extent and the spatial offset of receptive fields ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) for the <span id="S2.T4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DC-compensated</span>
“master key filters” 7 and 8 according to (<a href="#S2.E69" title="In 2.4 Reducing the bias in the estimates of the spatial variance of the Gaussian-smoothing-like receptive fields by DC-compensation ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E70" title="In 2.4 Reducing the bias in the estimates of the spatial variance of the Gaussian-smoothing-like receptive fields by DC-compensation ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
