<p id="S3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with numerical values of these entities shown in
Table <a href="#S3.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Note: ‣ 3 Modelling the 8 “master key filters” in terms of idealized scale-space operations ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>
based on the numerical values of the variances in
Table <a href="#S2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 2.6 Estimating variance parameters of receptive fields from weighted spatial spread measures ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows visualizations
of the corresponding idealized receptive fields.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_centering ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\hat{\sigma}_{x,i}=\operatorname{argmin}_{\sigma_{x,i}}|V_{xx,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})|)-V_{xx,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{norm}}(\cdot,\cdot)|)|\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmin</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.400em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.400em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>norm</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\hat{\sigma}_{x,i}=\operatorname{argmin}_{\sigma_{x,i}}|V_{xx,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})|)-V_{xx,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{norm}}(\cdot,\cdot)|)|\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(117)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\hat{\sigma}_{y,i}=\operatorname{argmin}_{\sigma_{y,i}}|V_{yy,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})|)-V_{yy,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{norm}}(\cdot,\cdot)|)|\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmin</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.400em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.400em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>norm</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\hat{\sigma}_{y,i}=\operatorname{argmin}_{\sigma_{y,i}}|V_{yy,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})|)-V_{yy,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{norm}}(\cdot,\cdot)|)|\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(118)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="S3.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Formal specification of the criteria used for determining
the scale estimates <math id="S3.F6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{x,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="0.890em">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{x,i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.F6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{y,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="0.890em">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{y,i}</annotation></semantics></math>
in the horizontal and vertical directions, by matching the diagonal
elements of the discrete variance-based spatial spread measures
between an idealized receptive field model
<math id="S3.F6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.110em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})</annotation></semantics></math>
according to (<a href="#S3.E93" title="In 3 Modelling the 8 “master key filters” in terms of idealized scale-space operations ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">93</span></a>)–(<a href="#S4.E131" title="In 4.1 The spaces spanned by linear combinations of the receptive field responses from the set of “master key filters” ‣ 4 Interpretation of the analysis and modelling results in terms of scale-space theory for spatial receptive fields ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">131</span></a>)
and (<a href="#S3.E100" title="In 3 Modelling the 8 “master key filters” in terms of idealized scale-space operations ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">100</span></a>) to the corresponding
discrete variance-based spatial spread measures
for the normalized versions <math id="S3.F6.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{norm}}(\cdot,\cdot)|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.110em">norm</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{norm}}(\cdot,\cdot)|)</annotation></semantics></math>
of the “master key filters”
according to (<a href="#S2.E63" title="In 2.3.3 Responses to monomials for the 8 “master key filters” operators ‣ 2.3 Measuring the accuracy in relation to centered or non-centered difference operators combined with spatial smoothing ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>)–(<a href="#S2.E68" title="In 2.3.3 Responses to monomials for the 8 “master key filters” operators ‣ 2.3 Measuring the accuracy in relation to centered or non-centered difference operators combined with spatial smoothing ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>)
and (<a href="#S2.E73" title="In 2.4 Reducing the bias in the estimates of the spatial variance of the Gaussian-smoothing-like receptive fields by DC-compensation ‣ 2 Measuring characteristic properties of the 8 “master key filters” in terms of spatial spread measures and responses to lower-order polynomials ‣ Modelling and analysis of the 8 filters from the ”master key filters hypothesis” for depthwise-separable deep networks in relation to idealized receptive fields based on scale-space theory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>). The parameter <math id="S3.F6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
specifies the spatial extent if the discrete weighting
kernel used for computing the weighted variance-based
spatial spread measures, and is provided as prior information,
chosen as <math id="S3.F6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all the filters.
(Note that since the idealized receptive field models
<math id="S3.F6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.110em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})</annotation></semantics></math> are
separable with respect to the Cartesian coordinate directions <math id="S3.F6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S3.F6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, the vertical parameter <math id="S3.F6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{y,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{y,1}</annotation></semantics></math> does
influence the estimate of the horizontal diagonal element
<math id="S3.F6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{xx,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.560em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.110em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{xx,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})|)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, the horizontal parameter <math id="S3.F6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x,1}</annotation></semantics></math> does
not influence the estimate of the vertical diagonal element
<math id="S3.F6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{yy,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.560em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext mathsize="1.110em">ideal</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{yy,|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{0},\sigma_{0})|}(|h_{i,\scriptsize\mbox{ideal}}(\cdot,\cdot;\;\sigma_{x,1},\sigma_{y,1})|)</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></figcaption>
</figure>
